 | DELETE | `/projects/{pid}/tasks/{tid}` | → 204 |
+| DELETE | `/orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}` | offboarding: removes the user from every project of the org → 204 |
+
+`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}` is for org admins of `{orgID}` only (a
+non-admin gets 403; another organization 404; a user who is not in the
+organization 404). It deletes the user's memberships in all of the
+organization's projects, archived ones included, and unassigns the tasks
+assigned to them there so the "assignee is a member" rule keeps holding.
+The user itself is kept.
 
